# =============================================================================
# NFTBan - P12-FPA registered rule-comment drift (boot projection vs canonical schema)
# =============================================================================
# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
#
# WHAT THIS FILE IS
# Each non-comment line is one rule-comment string that currently differs between
# the SHIPPED BOOT PROJECTION (install/nftables/nftables.conf) and the CANONICAL
# SCHEMA rendered with its install-time fallbacks (install/nftables/nftables.conf.tpl).
# check-firewall-projection-authority.sh P4 fails on any divergence NOT listed here.
#
# WHY THESE EXIST AND ARE NOT SIMPLY FIXED
# The boot projection ships as a DEB conffile and RPM %config(noreplace). Editing a
# shipped conffile makes the package manager treat the change as an operator conflict:
# every upgrade becomes an interactive prompt and unattended installs abort. This
# project has already had that failure once. Commit 6af9fe9f corrected the same wrong
# "per IP" wording in cli/lib/nftban/lib/nft_schema.sh and explicitly declined to touch
# these two files for that reason.
#
# THE SUBSTANTIVE DEFECT BEHIND THE FIRST SIX ENTRIES
# `ct count over N` counts connections HOST-WIDE, not per source address. The boot
# projection tells the operator "per IP", which is wrong, and that text is loaded into
# the kernel and read back by `nft list ruleset`. The canonical schema already carries
# the corrected wording. So the two projections disagree about what the same rule means.
#
# THE LAST FOUR ENTRIES are benign provenance-wording differences, registered only so
# that P4 can fail on anything NEW.
#
# ⛔ THIS REGISTRY MAY ONLY SHRINK. It is P12-FPA migration debt: once the boot
# projection is GENERATED rather than shipped as a conffile, every line here is
# corrected by regeneration and this file must be emptied. Adding a row to make a new
# drift pass is the exact failure this guard exists to prevent — extend the canonical
# schema and regenerate instead.
#
# Registered 2026-08-28 (P12-FPA Phase 1). Population at registration: 10.
# =============================================================================
comment "HTTP(S): max 150 concurrent NEW conns (host-wide, not per IP)"
comment "HTTP(S): max 150 concurrent per IP"
comment "MAIL: max 150 concurrent NEW conns (host-wide, not per IP)"
comment "MAIL: max 150 concurrent per IP"
comment "SSH: max 15 concurrent NEW conns (host-wide, not per IP) — v1.145 PR-A set-driven"
comment "SSH: max 15 concurrent per IP — v1.145/v1.162 set-driven"
comment "SSH ports for set-driven brute-force rate-limit"
comment "SSH ports for set-driven brute-force rate-limit (v1.162 §3.5 static-fallback)"
comment "SSH ports for set-driven brute-force rate-limit (v1.162 §3.5 static-fallback, v6)"
